Actually, I went with a slightly different path; it remembers which
monster you last targeted, and if that monster's still alive AND you're
still on the same level as the monster, the cursor starts at that point 
when you next a)pply the polearm; so you just hit '.' and it tries 
to hit again (standard range penalties/impossibilities apply).

If you've changed levels or if the monster dies, the cursor memory is
reset and it starts from 'you' again.

